# Line endings are otherwise left to each machine's core.autocrlf, which made the docs
# ratchet (test/contracts.test.js) platform-dependent: sync-docs.js inlines settings.json
# verbatim into autoconfig.docs.html, so a checkout with autocrlf=true put a stray \r on
# all 187 of its inlined lines and the byte-for-byte compare failed — on the three Windows
# CI runners only, while every ubuntu/macos job passed. `-text` means "never convert": the
# working file is the committed blob, byte for byte, on every platform.
#
# Deliberately scoped to the generator's inputs and its output rather than a repo-wide
# `text=auto`. Nine tracked blobs already carry CRLF — including token-guard.js (fleet-
# synced canonical), this generated HTML, and two .wav files — and normalizing those is a
# separate decision with a much larger blast radius than this bug.
.claude/docs/autoconfig.docs.html -text
.claude/settings.json -text
.claude/.mcp.json -text
